      "writtenOn": "2024-11-20T23:38:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When you\u0027re not touching the device most of the time it will turn off the CPU; you can see that when looking at a bugreport and opening it in the bug tool, see the \"device awake\" metric in the battery historian. On a random bugreport I had sitting around, out of 6 hours screen off time there are only 3 hours of uptime.\n\nSo it\u0027s not really the system_server being in deep sleep, it\u0027s the whole device turning off the CPU to save power. The system_server process is still alive in memory but there\u0027s no CPU cycles during that time. That\u0027s why holding a wakelock has a drastic effect on battery life :)\n\nYour new change LGTM at high level but I\u0027ll leave it up to your team for detailed review",
      "parentUuid": "ed2a02cb_70cd154b",
